      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): honor timeoutSeconds for dynamic tool calls when timeoutMs is absent",
        "body": "Fixes #98864.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nCodex dynamic tool calls forward tool arguments as JSON. Tools such as `sessions_send` expose an integer `timeoutSeconds` budget, but OpenClaw's outer dynamic-tool watchdog only honored `timeoutMs`. Seconds-only calls therefore inherited the generic 90-second watchdog, and a short inner timeout could race the outer bridge after target-resolution/setup work instead of returning its structured timeout result.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Use the existing dynamic-tool timeout owner for both the main run and side-question path; remove the duplicate side implementation.\n- Preserve exact `timeoutMs` precedence when it is supplied.\n- Interpret positive integer `timeoutSeconds` when `timeoutMs` is absent, with bounded 30-second outer headroom for setup and structured completion.\n- Keep the existing hard cap and configured media timeout behavior.\n- Reject fractional model-facing seconds rather than silently shortening them.\n\nThis is the correct ownership boundary: upstream Codex forwards dynamic-tool arguments unchanged and waits for the returned tool response, while OpenClaw owns the tool schema and watchdog policy. Relevant upstream source: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/be33f80bc65159c094ecd06bf155afa3061ce23d/codex-rs/protocol/src/dynamic_tools.rs#L45 and https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/be33f80bc65159c094ecd06bf155afa3061ce23d/codex-rs/core/src/tools/handlers/dynamic.rs#L127\n\n## User Impact\n\nSeconds-only dynamic tool calls now get the intended bounded budget on both Codex run paths. A tool can finish its own timeout handling and return structured state instead of being preempted by the generic bridge watchdog.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Full exact-head hosted CI: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28807346089\n- Focused regressions cover seconds fallback, exact millisecond precedence, malformed/fractional seconds, configured defaults, both main and side-question callers, and a `sessions_send` result after setup work.\n- Fresh autoreview completed with no accepted or actionable findings.\n- Review artifacts validated at the exact PR head with recommendation `READY FOR /prepare-pr` and zero findings.\n- Diff hygiene: `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`.\n",
